-- title:
--   Code generated by a matrix (random linear code model)
-- statement:
--   For a matrix $G\in\mathbb F_q^{n\times k}$, the **code generated by $G$** is its image
--
--   $$
--   C_G=\{Gv : v\in\mathbb F_q^k\}\subseteq\mathbb F_q^n .
--   $$
--
--   A **random linear code** of designed dimension $k$ and length $n$ is $C_G$ for a uniformly random $G$ (the random generating matrix model). No full-rank condition is imposed: a rank-deficient $G$ yields a code of dimension below $k$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `LinearMap.range G.mulVecLin`.
-- source:
--   Doron, Leonov, Mosheiff, Navas, Resch, Ribeiro, Discrepancy for Random Linear Codes, arXiv:2606.24471 (PDF sha256 f03561c3…), §2.1, p.12

import Mathlib

namespace RLCDiscrepancy

/-- **The code generated by a matrix** G ∈ F^{n×k}_q: its image {Gv : v ∈ F^k_q}. Doron, Leonov, Mosheiff, Navas, Resch, Ribeiro, *Discrepancy for Random Linear Codes*,
arXiv:2606.24471 (PDF sha256 f03561c3…), §2.1,
p.12: "a random linear code (RLC) of designed dimension k and length n over F_q is the image of a
uniformly random matrix G ∈ F^{n×k}_q."

**Formalization Note.** `LinearMap.range G.mulVecLin`, the column span, as a set: no full-rank
condition, so a rank-deficient `G` gives a code of dimension below `k`, as in the paper. -/
def rlc {F : Type*} [Field F] [Fintype F] {n k : ℕ} (G : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin k) F) : Submodule F (Fin n → F) :=
  LinearMap.range G.mulVecLin

end RLCDiscrepancy


